Distance and Speed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176032 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186175887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176032 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "6570253a-b05a-5721-9108-5fddab2b5388" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176136 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176820 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176136 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176136 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176136 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176136 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176136 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176136 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176136 #edb/ref 1045 "Speed as a Unit Rate" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176136 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186176820 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176136 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176136 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176136 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186176136 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "4cf8b9a9-4050-5d59-b451-2f66b157c8dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176820 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176820 #edb/ref 1061 36386 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176820 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "136b294f-0279-574d-9755-cfc8cb54f15d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176820 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186177044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176821 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176821 #edb/ref 1061 36387 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176821 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "aed82a50-e10d-539e-895f-797eb5220670" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176821 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186176030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176822 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176822 #edb/ref 1061 36388 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176822 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2e52190a-967b-5eee-8781-4b1c6cdc1bf7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176822 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186176031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176823 #edb/ref 1061 36389 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176823 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cb434a73-533d-5a74-927b-b8b1bf69153e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176823 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186176032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176824 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176824 #edb/ref 1061 36390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176824 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "02f9ad99-d474-59a2-b870-d4cc8af16598" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176824 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186177045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176825 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176825 #edb/ref 1061 36391 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176825 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1aec8595-c434-5eab-92bb-a1d9a3d99a15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176825 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186177046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177044 #edb/ref 1064 "**Speed** is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*.\n\nWe can calculate the speed of a moving object using the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed} = \\dfrac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nFor example, suppose that a car travels $80$ miles in $2$ hours at a constant rate. What is the speed of the car? \n\nTo find the speed (in miles per hour), we divide the number of miles, $80,$ by the number of hours, $2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{80}{2} = 40.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of the car is $40$ miles per hour." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177044 #edb/ref 1065 5959 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177044 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e151f782-1f59-5438-92a6-e678c9041d99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177044 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177045 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's return to the example of a car traveling at ${\\color{red}{40}}$ miles per hour. \n\nIf the car travels at this speed, it covers  a distance of ${\\color{red}{40}}$ miles *every hour*. Therefore, we can deduce the following:\n\n- after ${\\color{blue}{1}}$ hour, the car covers a distance of ${\\color{red}{40}}\\times{\\color{blue}{1}} = 40$ miles\n\n- after ${\\color{blue}{2}}$ hours, the car covers a distance of ${\\color{red}{40}}\\times{\\color{blue}{2}} = 80$ miles\n\n- after ${\\color{blue}{3}}$ hours, the car covers a distance of ${\\color{red}{40}}\\times{\\color{blue}{3}} = 120$ miles\n\n- after ${\\color{blue}{4}}$ hours, the car covers a distance of ${\\color{red}{40}}\\times{\\color{blue}{4}} = 160$ miles\n\n- $\\cdots$\n\nThis suggests the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{distance} = \\text{speed} \\times \\text{time}\n$$\n\nWe can use this formula to calculate the distance traveled by an object moving at a constant speed.\n\nFor instance, suppose an elevator traveled for $1.5$ minutes at a constant speed of $120$ feet per minute. What distance is covered by the elevator?\n\nThe speed is $120$ feet per minute. To find the distance covered in $1.5$ minutes, we multiply the speed by $1.5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{distance} & =\\text{speed}\\times \\text{time} \\\\  & =120\\times 1.5 \\\\  & =180.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elevator covered a distance of $180$ feet." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177045 #edb/ref 1065 5960 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177045 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "95f37ad7-7647-57e9-ae85-7a3dcab40f25" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177045 #edb/ref 1067 "Calculating the Distance Traveled by an Object" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177046 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's recall the formula relating distance to speed and time:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed} \\times \\text{time} = \\text{distance}\n$$\n\nUsing the relationship between multiplication and division, we can write this equation as\n\n$$\n\\text{time} = \\text{distance} \\div \\text{speed}\n$$\n\nwhich is equivalent to the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{time} = \\dfrac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{speed}}.\n$$\n\nWe can use this formula to calculate the time taken for an object moving at a particular speed to cover a certain distance. \n\nFor example, suppose a plane flew for $3\\,120$ kilometers at a constant speed of $520$ kilometers per hour. For how long was the plane in motion?\n\nTo determine the time the plane was in motion, we divide the distance, $3\\,120$ kilometers, by the speed, $520$ kilometers per hour. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{time} & =\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{speed}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\,120}{520} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\,120÷10}{520÷10} \\\\  & =\\frac{312}{52} \\\\  & =312÷52 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the plane was in motion for $6$ hours." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177046 #edb/ref 1065 5961 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177046 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "76064dfb-b2e4-56a5-95f7-2a97b1fb392b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177046 #edb/ref 1067 "Calculating the Total Time an Object is in Motion" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494299 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186495186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494299 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186495198 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494299 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186495208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494299 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186495235 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494299 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186495261 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494299 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494299 #edb/ref 1045 "Calculating Slopes of Straight Lines" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494299 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186495235 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494299 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494299 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494299 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "09d4bb8f-af12-534d-8b4d-e6041622fc03" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494336 #edb/ref 1080 "The slope is undefined" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494336 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494336 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "079a4194-4aeb-59b9-9a97-0a35913cad7f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494367 #edb/ref 1080 "Not enough information" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494367 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494367 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "18c4c7ec-5083-5460-99fa-85cb717da0d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494389 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494389 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494389 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "244abeff-5947-5d09-8904-4308c44b291c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494445 #edb/ref 1080 "Zero" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494445 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494445 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3d057346-e893-5b56-91c9-02634ef0bcb7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494464 #edb/ref 1080 "The slope is undefined" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494464 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494464 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "484abde8-3f23-5338-9c82-1f609256f392" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494469 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{7}{5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494469 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494469 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4b675aa5-7ca8-5a20-8b98-50a672fad62c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494486 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494486 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494486 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5346ccb5-d421-5f50-8754-3b145bc626f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494541 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{7}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494541 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494541 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6c973c76-cd0c-5576-8885-0c465bab546c" #edb/ref 1759218